{
  "_note": "Spec v2 §11 as amended by v2.1 §6: one visual language for hints. 'items' = the 'this is new' card (NewItemCard): the object's icon, then ▸ its effects as icons and numbers, framed and coloured by the item's 'tone' (tones: gain = good for you, threat = bad for you, use = something to shoot or aim at; each tone has a colour and a shape, so they read apart without colour too). The card and its marker share one clock (show_s); the marker is bound to the one object that triggered the hint and fades out in fade_s once that object is dead, passed or removed (it never moves to another one). Markers: a gang gets a toned ring that follows its survivors and the tone chip; an obstacle a small toned tag tag_y metres above it; every matching gate sign in the row a small toned sparkle (sparkle.dx/y = metres from the lane centre, px = size); a HUD power its button's toned pulse. No hand, no freeze. 'find' says which kind of object to bind when the hint event does not name one: obstacle kind, horde enemy (or the event's 'enemy'), gate op (+ unit/id), red gate, a hostage cage (an obstacle-style tag over it), a district hazard (no object on the street: the card alone; its strikes mark their lanes), or a HUD power button. A threat's number is what one landing can take at most (its cap as a share of the squad), like an obstacle's. An effect's number is 'text' (literal), or 'from': 'obj.<key>' (the bound object's own value: a level override shows; '<key>_pct' wins with fmt_pct when the object has it), 'units.<path>' (config/units.json) or 'value.<rank>' (Codex '= N constables' with the level's upgraded stats). default_tone colours a Tutorial ring that has no item (the Bottle Shot aims). 'hand.tip' = the fingertip in assets/ui/hand.png as a share of its size (tools/make_hand.py prints it).",
  "show_s": 2.6,
  "fade_s": 0.2,
  "tag_y": 2.1,
  "sparkle": {"dx": 0.95, "y": 2.35, "px": 20},
  "default_tone": "use",
